  "gotchas": [
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "No engine version file for sglang@0.0.0.dev1+g5f55db35e; no defaults could be dropped from the canonical config."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Boot lottery: this boot allocated the KV pool at the recipe-capped max-total-tokens of 1,048,576 (target cache torch.float8_e4m3fn, K 16.00 GB + V 16.00 GB; the DFlash2 draft cache is the same dtype at K 5.00 GB + V 5.00 GB), with mem-fraction-static 0.85 and the native 262144 window, leaving 17.13 GB free after CUDA-graph capture. The recipe documents boot-to-boot variance of about 8 percent on single-stream against under 2 percent run-to-run inside one server instance, so read a pool number out of the log of the boot it belongs to and size any A/B delta against 8 percent."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Five mamba state slots per request, not four. SGLang clamps max_running_requests to max_mamba_cache_size divided by 5, so the recipe sizes the GDN pool at 80 for a target of 16. That held here: the server log reports max_running_requests=16 with no clamp line, which is the check the recipe asks for after any change to either flag."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The GDN state pool costs more on this image than the recipe measured. At the same 80 slots with --mamba-ssm-dtype bfloat16 the server allocated conv_state 0.22 GB + ssm_state 5.70 GB + intermediate_ssm_state_cache 19.12 GB + intermediate_conv_window_cache 0.28 GB, so 25.3 GB against the 15.6 GB in the recipe memory table, and 17.13 GB free after load against its 20.6 GB. The recipe numbers came from a locally built image on an older SGLang; this ran the official lmsysorg/sglang:dev-cu13-qwen38-27b-dflash2, engine version 0.0.0.dev1+g5f55db35e. Budget the difference before raising the pool to the 160 the recipe calls the practical ceiling."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The recipe fetch script downloads both checkpoints into the real ~/.cache/huggingface, but the toolkit launcher it hands off to sets HF_HOME to the working directory it is started from, so following the two documented steps in order re-downloads about 25 GB into the toolkit directory. The weights were staged across as hardlinks instead. Hardlinks are safe here; symlinks are not, because the container bind-mounts that directory and an in-mount symlink to a host-only path makes it re-download and then fail with OSError File exists."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "A download pinned to a revision leaves no refs/main in the Hugging Face cache, and SGLang resolves the draft config in its early speculative-algorithm probe without a revision. refs/main was written for both repositories before the first start, pointing at the pinned snapshots, so the probe resolved locally and the server log shows no lookup for either."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The toolkit launcher builds its command line for EAGLE and the DFlash2 wrapper only appends overrides, so --speculative-num-steps 3 and --speculative-eagle-topk 1 are still on the command line under --speculative-algorithm DFLASH. SGLang resolved speculative_num_steps to 1 for DFlash2 and ignored the rest; the served args record what the server parsed, not what the wrapper passed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Draft tokens are set to 16, the recipe README step 6 optimum for interactive single-stream work. The recipe is explicit that the optima diverge and that 10 is the better setting for concurrent serving, worth 435 against 385 aggregate tok/s in its own sweep, so the c8 and c16 rows here are measured at the single-stream setting and are not this recipe at its concurrency optimum."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "This is the standalone launch path of README step 3 plus the step 5 and step 6 tuning passed through DF_EXTRA, not the SparkStation orchestration of step 4. The recipe measures the LiteLLM gateway overhead at zero (62.3 against 62.5 tok/s), and its own traps list the SparkStation supervisor restarting a healthy model mid-job when a long prefill cannot answer a 5 second health probe, which would corrupt the long-context rows. No systemd unit, supervisor or cockpit was installed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The server runs with no API key and with sleep_on_idle false, so unlike some recipes on this cell there is no idle wake-up cost on the first request after a gap. Every workload still ran after a warm-up request on an already-answering server."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Target revision 554ebba9 is the same revision the atlas quant entry nvfp4-fp4-lmhead pins, so no revision patch was needed. Passing it is still required: the recipe warns that downloading the right checkpoint does not make SGLang load it, and --revision has to be given to the server separately."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Speed rows force thinking off per request with chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false. Eval rows use the served default, which here is thinking on at full length, because the chat template comes from the target repository unmodified and sampling-defaults is model. The recipe warns that a small token cap with thinking on returns empty content with everything in reasoning_content, which reads as a quality regression: it scored one of its own 97.0 percent runs at 90.9 percent that way."
    }
  ],
